  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Face of the Border Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intended outcome of the project is that improved border crossing services performed by the State Border Guard Service (SBGS) will enable more efficient and faster movements for persons and goods across the border. The project will deliver in the following outputs:1. An automated human resource management system is rolled out allowing more efficient recruitment processes and enhance the management of human resources of border divisions; 2. Support for the recruitment and selection of SBGS staff is provided; 3. An enhanced training system for the SBGS is developed and implemented to facilitate the training of new and existing personnel in a more gender sensitive manner; 4. Adequate equipment has been provided to the SBGS in support of the intended changes to its human resource management system, training procedures and improved service delivery at border crossing points.</narrative>
  </description>
